src/backend/access/yb_scan/README

YB Scan Layer
=============

This directory implements scans of YB relations: heap's scan functions for YB
tables and the accessors that executor nodes still call on them, the low-level
scan primitives that the YB table and index access methods share, the scan
logic that the planner shares, the YB implementation of genam's systable
scans, ANALYZE row sampling, and single-row fetch by ybctid.  The headers that
the groups below list are all under src/include/access/.  Most of them are
implemented in this directory, but four are implemented in
src/backend/access/common/: yb_cost.h, yb_target.h, yb_lockrows.h, and
yb_parallel_scan.h.  #37428 and #37429 track reorganizing this directory and
those implementations by role.

Code above the access-method layer, such as executor nodes, the optimizer,
commands, and catalog and cache code, should reach YB relations only through
the interfaces upstream code uses for any table or index access method:
tableam, the index AM interface, and genam's systable functions.  YB extends
those interfaces where it needs to, as with table_beginscan_*_yb() and the
yb_ammightrecheck index AM callback, rather than going around them.  The write
path, which goes around tuple_insert, tuple_update, and tuple_delete, is not
structured this way yet.  The groups below sort the headers by how they relate
to that rule.  The comment at the top of each header says what belongs in it
and, where only some code may include it, which code that is.

Headers
-------

Internal to the access methods:

  yb_scan_core.h
  yb_sys_scan_base.h

Extending tableam:

  yb_table_scan_options.h

Execution logic that the planner shares instead of copying:

  yb_scan_plan.h

The YB cost model, mostly planner code that sits under access/ for historical
reasons:

  yb_cost.h

Building pggate requests, used by the access methods and by some code above
them:

  yb_target.h

Entry points outside the AM interfaces, some of them interim bypasses tracked
in #36168:

  yb_special_scans.h

Bypasses of an AM interface still to be removed, tracked in #36168:

  yb_table_scan.h
  yb_lockrows.h
  yb_parallel_scan.h (the sequential scan side)

Avoid adding a bypass, including a new entry point in one of the bypass
headers above.  When one is unavoidable, declare it in the header of the
bypass it extends or in a new src/include/access/yb_*.h header if it is a new
kind of bypass.  That header's comment should name the files that may include
it.  It should also say why no AM interface fits or cite the issue that tracks
removing the bypass.
